00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:25.520
Laffer is the guy after whom the Laffer Curve is&nbsp;
named. This is the relationship between the rate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:33.120
of taxation and total government tax revenue. The&nbsp;
idea is if government tax the tax rate is zero,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:39.120
then the government takes in no tax revenue. If&nbsp;
the tax rate is 100, the government also takes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:44.160
in no tax revenue because why would anyone do any&nbsp;
work if all of your money goes to taxes? So then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:51.040
once you understand that, you can find some&nbsp;
point on the curve that maximizes government tax&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:58.960
revenue. Laffer is view as a supply sider. Is that&nbsp;
to maximize tax revenue, you go with a lower tax&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:04.800
because people are more productive and therefore&nbsp;
government revenue goes up. He's the concept is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:10.240
fair concept. The way that Laffer applies, it&nbsp;
applies his own economic views to it doesn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:15.280
really make any sense. Now, Trump loves this guy.&nbsp;
